    "title": "Seymour Duncan: 2 humbuckers, 3-way toggle, 1 volume, 1 tone push/pull split",
    "creator": "Pickup Lab; reference: Seymour Duncan",
    "sourceUrl": "https://www.seymourduncan.com/images/wiring-diagrams/2H_3G_1V_1TppSPL.pdf",
    "permission": "Seymour Duncan encourages sharing these wiring diagrams freely; commercial use requires prior written permission. LIMITATIONS: Two blade poles represent the 3-way toggle, not physical terminals. Generic series humbuckers use logical A START/A END/B START/B END/SHIELD instead of lead colors/polarity. Bridge ground, cable, and load omitted; no bridge terminal exists. Logical pot lugs and linear scale omit orientation and audio taper. The PDF 0.047 uF capacitor uses the model's 47 nF setting."
  },
